What is GitOps, and why are so many teams using it today?

In simple words, GitOps is a way of managing your infrastructure and application deployments using Git — just like how developers manage their code.

Here’s why GitOps is a game-changer:

✅ Everything is in Git – Your entire system’s setup is stored in Git, so you always know what’s running and what changed.

✅ Automatic deployments – When you update something in Git, it can automatically get deployed. No more manual steps!

✅ Safe and secure – Every change is tracked and approved through pull requests, making it easier to audit and control.

✅ Easy rollback – If something breaks, you can go back to a previous working version just by reverting a commit.

✅ Perfect for Kubernetes – Tools like Argo CD and Flux make it easy to apply GitOps in cloud-native environments.

GitOps helps teams move faster with less risk — and once you set it up, it feels like magic! ✨
